<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  CometGUI SpotBugs exclusion filter (phase 01, work unit 2).

  POLICY, which is the point of this file existing while empty:

  * SpotBugs runs at effort=Max, threshold=Low - the most sensitive setting it
    has.  That is deliberate: the gate was installed while the tree was almost
    empty, so no later phase inherits a defect the analyser was never tuned to
    see.
  * A SpotBugs finding is fixed in the code by default.  An exclusion is the
    last resort, not the first, and it is for findings that are *wrong about
    this code*, never for findings that are inconvenient.
  * Every <Match> below must carry a comment giving: the bug pattern, the exact
    class or method it applies to, why the finding does not hold here, and the
    date and phase that added it.  A Match with no such comment is a defect in
    this file.
  * Exclusions are narrow.  Match on <Bug pattern="..."/> AND <Class .../> (or
    a specific <Method .../>).  A bare <Bug pattern=".."/> that silences a
    pattern across the whole product is a weakening of a gate, and so is
    raising <threshold> to make findings disappear.

  As of 2026-08-29 there is exactly one exclusion, below.
-->
<FindBugsFilter
    xmlns="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="https://github.com/spotbugs/filter/3.0.0 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/spotbugs/spotbugs/master/spotbugs/etc/findbugsfilter.xsd">

  <!--
    NP_NULL_PARAM_DEREF_NONVIRTUAL / NP_NULL_PARAM_DEREF /
    NP_NONNULL_PARAM_VIOLATION, in test sources only.  Added 2026-08-29,
    phase 01 unit 2.

    WHY IT DOES NOT HOLD HERE.  A test that proves a method rejects null has to
    pass it null.  BuildIdentityTest.FromProperties.rejectsNullProperties does
    exactly that and asserts on the resulting NullPointerException message;
    SpotBugs reports the test's whole purpose as the bug.  There is no
    annotation or code change that removes the finding without removing the
    test, and CONTRIBUTING.rst requires the rejected input to be proved rather
    than assumed.

    WHY IT IS NARROW ENOUGH.  It is confined to source files named *Test.java,
    and to the three patterns that describe a deliberately-null argument.  It
    does not touch main sources, where a null passed to a non-null parameter is
    a real defect and still fails the build.  SpotBugs still analyses test code
    for everything else; includeTests stays true.

    IF YOU ARE HERE TO ADD A SECOND EXCLUSION: read the policy above first.  A
    finding on main sources is fixed in the code.
  -->
  <Match>
    <Source name="~.*Test\.java"/>
    <Or>
      <Bug pattern="NP_NULL_PARAM_DEREF_NONVIRTUAL"/>
      <Bug pattern="NP_NULL_PARAM_DEREF"/>
      <Bug pattern="NP_NONNULL_PARAM_VIOLATION"/>
    </Or>
  </Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
